Frame-generation diagnosis dump (DCS Control, 2026-11-26, dev only): what the MV composition decided per pixel.
Off unless the process has XRFG_DEV_FG_DIAG=1 and a folder (XRFG_DEV_FG_DIAG_DIR, else the capture layer's
RIGTAP_DIR); without them nothing is made and every composition is the build before this patch, byte for byte.
- A trigger file <folder>\fgdiag.txt (pairs, every, delay_ms, seconds, tag, window=l,r,u,d tangents, eye) starts a
  session; it is renamed fgdiag.taken-<n>.txt. From delay_ms on, each synthesizer with that eye dumps up to `pairs`
  of its pairs with DCS's MVs into <folder>\fgdiag<n>_<tag>\ (s<owner>_p<k>.bin + .json, s<owner>_pairs.csv).
- A dumped pair binds the _extras twin of its composition (the records' code is compiled there only; with no quality
  bit it composes exactly as the plain one) with UseGameMotion bit 28 on the dumped view. Its u0 is then the
  synthesizer's diagnosis buffer: the counters copied in before and back after (their semantics unchanged), the dump
  rectangle and magic written at byte 128 (WriteBufferImmediate), one 8-byte record per pixel and output from 256:
  the path (cockpit mask, no usable MV, samples outside, gather MV, scatter MV), the gather's cell flags and class,
  the scatter candidate's class, consistency and choice, the sky rule, the still-content guard, the strict check,
  the final weight, the colour check's weight, the disagreement and the mask value.
- After the composition the records, the resampled grid's three slices and the scatter's two of that view, and the
  frame's MV and class atlases (as the consumer copied them) go into a readback ring entry; a writer thread of its
  own (below normal priority) writes them once the slot's fence has passed. A full ring skips the pair (noted).
